        <briefdescription>
<para>Attempt to acquire the mutex without blocking. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>If the mutex is already locked by another task and <computeroutput>task</computeroutput> has higher priority (numerically lower value) than the owner, the owner&apos;s priority is automatically boosted.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Single-scheduler (AMP) scope: all scheduled tasks (<computeroutput>task-&gt;sched != NULL</computeroutput>) acquiring or contending on a mutex must belong to the same <computeroutput><ref refid="structSYN__Sched" kindref="compound">SYN_Sched</ref></computeroutput> instance (<computeroutput><ref refid="syn__defs_8h_1ac74d19fd322a889de9e46b79fb277c00a665ca721c73f662b5ceafe25aff4663b" kindref="member">SYN_INVALID_PARAM</ref></computeroutput> otherwise). Use <computeroutput><ref refid="syn__port__spinlock_8h" kindref="compound">syn_port_spinlock.h</ref></computeroutput> or SPSC <computeroutput>syn_mailbox</computeroutput> across AMP cores.</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>mutex</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to mutex structure. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>task</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
